.TH AVR\-WORKFLOW\-RUN 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-workflow-run \- Trigger a workflow_dispatch event.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr workflow run
[OPTIONS] WORKFLOW
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trigger a workflow_dispatch event.
.PP
WORKFLOW can be an Avrea workflow ID (wfl-... or awf-...), a GitHub numeric workflow ID, a workflow path, or the workflow's display name. Bare filenames (build.yml) select GitHub Actions; use the full .avrea/workflows/build.yml path for Avrea CI.
.PP
Native -f inputs use the workflow's declared types. JSON preserves booleans and numbers. A receipt identifies the exact native run. If a response is lost, use the printed retry command to recover the same invocation with its resolved ref, inputs and --idempotency-key. --no-watch prints the accepted ref and commit plus a command to resume following a pending native dispatch.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr workflow run build.yml
    avr workflow run "Build and Deploy" --ref feat/x
    avr workflow run wfl-abc123 -f env=prod -f region=eu
    echo '{"env":"prod"}' | avr workflow run build.yml --json
    avr workflow run build.yml --watch --exit-status
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIWORKFLOW_IDENTIFIER\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-ref\fR \fITEXT\fR
Branch or tag to run at. Defaults to the repository's default branch.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-raw\-field\fR \fITEXT\fR
Workflow input: key=value (repeatable). (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Read a JSON object of inputs from stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fIUUID\fR
For Avrea CI, reuse this key to retry the same invocation.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-watch\fR / \fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-no\-watch\fR
Poll for the new run and watch it until completion. Pass --no-watch / -W to return immediately. (default: True)
.TP
\fB\-\-exit\-status\fR
With --watch, exit non-zero if the run failed.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
With --watch, refresh interval in seconds. (default: 3)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-workflow (1),
.BR avr-workflow-list (1),
.BR avr-workflow-view (1)
